From 8ba72ad1f44a6662f929b392af043cee91084955 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FVOCI <150913557+fvoci@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 08:50:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix(web): ask before saving my value over a field someone
 else changed after a task conflict (D-94)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

"내 입력으로 다시 저장" merged my input onto the latest version but kept
my value on a field both sides changed without asking. Following D-94,
mergeForm now names the clashing fields (the estimate text and tags are
compared the same way refresh() does). With no clash it saves right away
at the latest version: untouched fields take the latest values, my edits
stay. With clashes it shows, inside the conflict notice, each field's
current server value and my value and asks whether to overwrite; cancel
sends nothing and keeps my input. The save is checked against the latest
version, so a further change answers 409 again and the notice shows the
newer version while my input stays; the next try merges onto that
version. Any failure keeps my input.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
